# Local docs clone (~400MB). Cloned on request by the `/sn-init` SKILL (the agent, not the
# script — scripts/sn-init never clones). Refresh: `git -C vendor/ServiceNowDocs pull`.
vendor/

# SDK build artifacts — regenerate with `now-sdk build`.
# Fluent projects are not only under apps/: the loop builds in place under
# enhancements/<number>/, and one of those was 544MB of node_modules. Match anywhere.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/target/
**/.npm-cache/

# Evidence that is large or binary: screenshots and terminal recordings are part of a
# package's evidence manifest but are not versioned. The package file records their
# names and sizes.
**/evidence/*.png
**/evidence/*.cast
**/evidence/*.mov

# Documents the requester attached to the ticket. The loop downloads them here and reads
# them; they belong to the business unit that sent them, not to this repo. Read in place,
# never commit. This is the recipient's confidential material, not ours.
**/handoff-in/

# Never. Credentials live in ~/.snpdi/env, outside the repo entirely.
.env*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
.snpdi

# Generated grounding — every instance generates its own via /sn-map; never shipped.
codex/instance-profile.md
__pycache__/

# Working state of the current build-out — lives with the experiment's own record, not in
# the shipped product. A fresh clone starts with CLAUDE.md and the codex, not our head-state.
HEAD_STATE.md
data/
.agents/

# The control plane ships as a product; its RUN RECORD does not. Same placement test as the
# rest of the repo: could a stranger with their own instance use this? → ship it. Does it only
# make sense to someone who knows why we did it? → it stays local. Receipts, screenshots and
# the dated build journal are ours; the source, the runner and the codex are theirs.
apps/ai-development-control-plane/evidence/
apps/ai-development-control-plane/BUILD_JOURNAL.md
apps/ai-development-control-plane/NEXT_AGENT_PROMPT.md

# Recording leftovers
*.cast
*.orig
.DS_Store
